 "critic": "Most traces supply event categories without concrete motives, objects, demands, or usable next steps. Requests to act against the asker remain especially difficult to understand. Causal pointers establish asserted connections but often do not explain them; simultaneous or reversed reporting further obscures some chains. A closing label such as resolved, betrayal, or reckoning supplies little payoff without the actual consequence. Completed contracts also conceal methods and findings, particularly surveillance and missing-person inquiries. Repeated structures make participants interchangeable. Eddies, shards, gangs, and local routes support Night City, but many traces could occur anywhere. The modest repair and escort jobs have the clearest practical reasons and proportionate endings. Explicit refusals provide fair stopping points even when little story develops."
